        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0b011f9f-e56a-5034-8e2a-432046136106",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Texas Raiders, Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress, B-17G-95-DL\n- Places: Conroe, Texas, Conroe North Houston Regional Airport, General Aviation Services, Australia, Melbourne, Philippines\n- People: Douglas MacArthur\n- Organizations: United States Army Air Corps\n- Concepts: heavy bombers\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1930s, Boeing developed the B-17 Flying Fortress as a four-engine heavy bomber for the United States Army Air Corps.\n- From its introduction in 1938, the Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress underwent numerous design advances and became the third-most produced bomber of all time, behind the B-24 and the multirole Ju 88.\n- On 21 March, Douglas MacArthur and his party completed their escape from the Philippines by flying to Australia in two Boeing B-17 Flying Fortresses and then arriving in Melbourne by train.\n- Texas Raiders is an American Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress and a Douglas-Long Beach built B-17G-95-DL.\n- Texas Raiders is hangared at General Aviation Services at Conroe North Houston Regional Airport in Conroe, Texas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
